/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (  Each component plays a crucial role in the overall functionality of the sound-activated light control system. The sound sensor detects the sound, the Arduino processes the input and controls the relay, the relay switches the light, and the battery powers the system. Jumper wires and the breadboard are used for connecting and prototyping the system, enabling a functional and efficient automation setup based on sound detection. The Sound-Activated Light Control System presents an innovative approach to automating lighting based on sound detection, offering a simple yet effective solution for hands-free light control. The system utilizes a combination of cost-effective components such as the sound sensor, Arduino microcontroller, relay module, and light, with power provided by a battery. These components work together seamlessly to create an intuitive and energy-efficient system. )
/E (  Each component plays a crucial role in the overall functionality of the sound-activated light control system. The sound sensor detects the sound, the Arduino processes the input and controls the relay, the relay switches the light, and the battery powers the system. Jumper wires and the breadboard are used for connecting and prototyping the system, enabling a functional and efficient automation setup based on sound detection. The Sound-Activated Light Control System presents an innovative approach to automating lighting based on sound detection, offering a simple yet effective solution for hands-free light control. The system utilizes a combination of cost-effective components such as the sound sensor, Arduino microcontroller, relay module, and light, with power provided by a battery. These components work together seamlessly to create an intuitive and energy-efficient system. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
