/T ( and allowing current to flow to the light source. This action turns the light on. Conversely, if the system is designed to turn off the light after a delay or upon the detection of another sound, the relay can open its contacts, cutting off the power supply to the light and turning it off. The relay provides crucial isolation between the low-voltage Arduino system and the high-voltage light circuit, ensuring the safety of the system and preventing electrical hazards. )
